    {
      "id": "be-s8-cost-concepts-c3",
      "heading": "Average and marginal cost",
      "explanation_md": "- **ATC = C(Q)/Q**, and **ATC = AVC + AFC**\n- **AVC = VC(Q)/Q**\n- **AFC = FC/Q**\n- **MC = ΔC/ΔQ**, the extra cost of one more unit\n\nOn the graph, **AFC keeps falling** (the same fixed cost spread over more units). AVC and ATC are **U-shaped**, with ATC above AVC. **MC cuts AVC and ATC at their minimum points**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "ATC = AVC + AFC; AFC = FC/Q falls forever; MC cuts AVC and ATC at their lowest points.",
      "clarification": null,
