    {
      "id": "be-s8-cost-concepts-c5",
      "heading": "Worked question: the cost table",
      "explanation_md": "Fixed cost is **₹100** at every output. TC = TFC + TVC, AFC = TFC/Q, AVC = TVC/Q, ATC = TC/Q, MC = change in TC.\n\n| Q | TVC | TC | AFC | AVC | ATC | MC |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 60 | 160 | 100 | 60 | 160 | 60 |\n| 2 | 100 | 200 | 50 | 50 | 100 | 40 |\n| 3 | 135 | 235 | 33.3 | 45 | 78.3 | 35 |\n| 4 | 180 | 280 | 25 | 45 | 70 | 45 |\n| 5 | 240 | 340 | 20 | 48 | 68 | 60 |\n| 6 | 315 | 415 | 16.7 | 52.5 | 69.2 | 75 |\n\nNotice MC is lowest at Q = 3, AVC is lowest at Q = 3 and 4, and ATC is lowest at Q = 5.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-cost-table-100"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Build the table column by column; MC is the change in TC, not TC/Q.",
